// Robust COGO Test Script - Figure-based Horizontal Curves
// This script thoroughly tests the creation of complex curvilinear 
// geometries, relying heavily on the FIG command (CONT alias)
// to assemble figures, and the XC command to simulate curves.

CLEAR
LOG ON

// ==========================================
// 1. Establish Alignment Control Points
// ==========================================
// Let's create a main alignment path with several PI (Point of Intersection) points
NE 1 5000.000 5000.000 "Start of Alignment"
NE 2 6000.000 5500.000 "PI 1"
NE 3 6000.000 7000.000 "PI 2"
NE 4 5000.000 7500.000 "PI 3"
NE 5 4500.000 7000.000 "PI 4"
NE 6 4500.000 6000.000 "End of Alignment"

// Compute Azimuths and Distances for reference
INV 1 2
INV 2 3
INV 3 4
INV 4 5
INV 5 6

// ==========================================
// 2. Centerline Figure Construction (using FIG command)
// ==========================================
// We will build a continuous centerline route using the FIG alias.
BEG CENTERLINE

// Add the Start Point
FIG 1

// First Curve Segment (Simulating a long curve with XC commands)
// Synthesized curve points are auto-appended to the figure
XC ZD (BULB) 200.0 30.0000 50.0
XC ZD (BULB) 200.0 40.0000 50.0
XC ZD (BULB) 200.0 50.0000 50.0

// Tie back into next PI
FIG 2

// Second Curve Segment (Reverse curve simulation)
XC ZD (BULB) 300.0 120.0000 75.0
XC ZD (BULB) 300.0 110.0000 75.0
XC ZD (BULB) 300.0 100.0000 75.0

// Next PI
FIG 3

// Third Curve Segment
XC ZD (BULB) 150.0 200.0000 40.0
XC ZD (BULB) 150.0 220.0000 40.0
XC ZD (BULB) 150.0 240.0000 40.0

// Next PI
FIG 4

// Standard straight segment to PI 5
FIG 5

// Final Curve to the exit
XC BD (BULB) 500.0 3 45.0000 100.0
XC BD (BULB) 500.0 3 55.0000 100.0
XC BD (BULB) 500.0 3 65.0000 100.0

// Tie into the end
FIG 6

// End Centerline Assembly
END

// Validate the geometry closure and area of the complex curve route
MAPCHECK CENTERLINE

// ==========================================
// 3. Right of Way Figure Construction (Offsets)
// ==========================================
// Let's create an offset bounding box using standard point definitions
// and test closing a complete loop strictly with FIG commands.

NE 101 4900.000 5000.000 "ROW Start SW"
NE 102 6100.000 5500.000 "ROW PI 1 NW"
NE 103 6100.000 7000.000 "ROW PI 2 NE"
NE 104 5000.000 7600.000 "ROW PI 3 SE"

BEG ROW_BOUNDARY
FIG 101
FIG 102
FIG 103
FIG 104
FIG 101
END

MAPCHECK ROW_BOUNDARY

// ==========================================
// 4. Cul-de-Sac Loop Construction
// ==========================================
// Build a standalone looped contour with extensive curve points
BEG CUL_DE_SAC
FIG 5
// 360 degree simulated curve sweep
XC ZD (BULB) 60.0 0.0000 20.0
XC ZD (BULB) 60.0 45.0000 20.0
XC ZD (BULB) 60.0 90.0000 20.0
XC ZD (BULB) 60.0 135.0000 20.0
XC ZD (BULB) 60.0 180.0000 20.0
XC ZD (BULB) 60.0 225.0000 20.0
XC ZD (BULB) 60.0 270.0000 20.0
XC ZD (BULB) 60.0 315.0000 20.0
FIG 5
END

MAPCHECK CUL_DE_SAC

// Output Final Verifications
LIST PTS
SAVE fig_curve_comprehensive.cogo
LOG OFF
